  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q9-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Two $\\$1$ coins and two $\\$2$ coins are placed in a bag. A player draws coins without replacement until they receive a $\\$2$ coin. How much does the player expect to receive in total?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$\\frac{8}{3}$, or approximately $\\$2.67$.\n\nWeight the possible total returns by their probabilities.",
      "worked": "Let $X$ be the total return in dollars. The possible totals are $2$, $3$ and $4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X=2)&=\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac12\\\\P(X=3)&=\\frac{2}{4}\\times\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac13\\\\P(X=4)&=\\frac{2}{4}\\times\\frac{1}{3}\\times\\frac{2}{2}=\\frac16\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=2\\times\\frac12+3\\times\\frac13+4\\times\\frac16\\\\E(X)&=\\frac83\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe expected total return is $\\$\\frac83$, approximately $\\$2.67$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
